y with human leaders should such an  alliance prove worthwhile at the end of  act 1  in The Witcher 2 you have to decide  whose side you're basically on this is  the witcher two's biggest decision if  you side with roche you go down what's  called roches path going with your vez  goes down your vets path in either case  you confront a series of choices that  you do not confront should you go down  the other's path furthermore the next  choice you make in this conversation on  The Witcher 3 depends on what choice you  choose here so if you chose your vus  path your third choice in The Witcher 3  in this conversation is this did you  save Tris at the LOC moines summit or  did you lift the spell that held Saskia  so if you didn't know Triss Merigold is  gerelds primary romantic interest in The  Witcher games and a pretty great  sorceress Saskia is a beloved warrior  who led a revolt when King Hensel tried  to invade her land at this stage of The  Witcher 2 Tris is imprisoned in a war  camp and saskia who's actually a  shape-shifting dragon is under control  of a powerful sorceress named philippa  eilhart if you chose Tris not only did  you get to have some fun in the camp but  you also got to see Tris accuse Sheila  de Tan servile another powerful mage of  being the puppet master behind full  tests death if you choose to release  Saskia from her curse she regains her  free will but there are damaging  repercussions for mages who now become  the victims of a witch hunt now if you  chose Roach's path in the question  number 2 your third choice is as follows  did you save Tristram her nilfgaardian  prison or did you save Anais lavallette  now  Anais lavallette is Aryans half-sister  and she is the daughter of king foltest  that means that nie is the true heir two  full tests thrown she's captured and  held by hensel's forces and should you  choose to rescue her you must again make  a choice handing her either / - the  kingdom of redania or - tameria if you  rescue Tris ho